IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 4.
-- Part 4, Division 3 (shares): ss 64 to 68: voting rights, classes with different voting rights, differences in calls, reserve liability, share warrants, the use of share capital to pay issue expenses, and shares issued for no consideration.
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE (BOOLEAN, NUMBER ...): JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga1)") has the rule of 2026-10-29 and the two readings "for a lawyer".
-- "Subject to" a provision the encoding does not own (s 21, s 76J, another written law) is a delegation: the function answers NOTHING when the supplied fact says the other provision applies (fork F-X2).

§ `Section 64: rights and powers attaching shares`

-- (1) the right to one vote on a poll, with the exceptions the text names. JUST TRUE is the default right; JUST FALSE is the constitution having negated it as subsection (3) lets it.
-- src:6664 | 64.—(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), sections 21 and 76J,
-- src:6665 | and any written law to the contrary, a share in a company confers on
-- src:6666 | the holder of the share the right to one vote on a poll at a meeting of
-- src:6667 | the company on any resolution.
-- src:6677 | (3) Subject to subsection (4) and section 64A, a right specified in
-- src:6678 | subsection (1) may be negated, altered, or added to by the constitution
-- src:6679 | of the company.
@ref s 64(1) (src:6664-6679)
GIVEN `the thing is a share in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 21, section 76J or a written law to the contrary provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company negates the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) protects the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the thing is a share in a company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a share in a company" -- a thing that is not a share in a company is not covered
    ELSE (IF `section 21, section 76J or a written law to the contrary provides otherwise`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (delegated): "Subject to subsections (2) and (3), sections 21 and 76J, and any written law to the contrary" -- the answer sits in those provisions (fork F-X2)
          ELSE (IF `the constitution of the company negates the right` AND (NOT `subsection (4) protects the right`)
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a right specified in subsection (1) may be negated, altered, or added to by the constitution of the company" -- the constitution has negated it (fork F-RT1)
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- (2) the constitution's call-payment condition.
-- src:6671 | (2) A company’s constitution may provide that a member is not
-- src:6672 | entitled to vote unless all calls or other sums personally payable by
-- src:6673 | the member in respect of shares in the company have been paid.
@ref s 64(2) (src:6671-6673)
GIVEN `the constitution provides that a member is not entitled to vote unless all calls or other sums personally payable by the member in respect of shares in the company have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all calls or other sums personally payable by the member in respect of shares in the company have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2) the member is not entitled to vote by reason of the constitution's provision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the constitution provides that a member is not entitled to vote unless all calls or other sums personally payable by the member in respect of shares in the company have been paid`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company's constitution may provide that" -- a grant the constitution has not used; the subsection says nothing of a constitution without the provision
    ELSE (IF `all calls or other sums personally payable by the member in respect of shares in the company have been paid`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member is not entitled to vote unless all calls or other sums personally payable by the member in respect of shares in the company have been paid" -- the "unless" is met (grant ruling, limit 2)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (3) what the constitution may do to the right.
-- src:6677 | (3) Subject to subsection (4) and section 64A, a right specified in
-- src:6678 | subsection (1) may be negated, altered, or added to by the constitution
-- src:6679 | of the company.
@ref s 64(3) (src:6677-6679)
GIVEN `the constitution negates or alters the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution adds to the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) protects the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 64A prevents it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` MEANS
    IF `the constitution negates or alters the right` AND `subsection (4) protects the right`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (4) and section 64A, a right specified in subsection (1) may be negated, altered, or added to" -- subsection (4) takes the protected right out of the power (the text of (4) says "may not be negated or altered")
    ELSE (IF `section 64A prevents it`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (delegated): "Subject to subsection (4) and section 64A" -- the answer sits in section 64A (fork F-X2)
          ELSE (IF `the constitution negates or alters the right` OR `the constitution adds to the right`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be negated, altered, or added to by the constitution" -- a grant the constitution has not used

-- (4) the protected right of a holder of a specified share. The function answers "may be negated or altered": JUST FALSE is protected.
-- src:6683 | (4) Despite subsection (3), the right of a holder of a specified share
-- src:6684 | of a company to at least one vote on a poll at a meeting of the
-- src:6685 | company on the following resolutions may not be negated or altered:
-- src:6687 | (a) a resolution to wind up the company voluntarily under
-- src:6688 | section 160 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:6689 | Dissolution Act 2018; or
-- src:6691 | (b) a resolution to vary any right attached to a specified share
-- src:6692 | and conferred on the holder.
@ref s 64(4) (src:6683-6692)
GIVEN `the share is a specified share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a resolution to wind up the company voluntarily under section 160 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a resolution to vary any right attached to a specified share and conferred on the holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(4) the right of the holder of the specified share to at least one vote on a poll on the resolution may be negated or altered` MEANS
    IF    `the share is a specified share`
      AND (   `the resolution is a resolution to wind up the company voluntarily under section 160 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
           OR `the resolution is a resolution to vary any right attached to a specified share and conferred on the holder`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the right of a holder of a specified share of a company to at least one vote on a poll at a meeting of the company on the following resolutions may not be negated or altered"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the following resolutions" -- another share or another resolution is not covered

-- (5) "specified share".
-- src:6696 | (5) In subsection (4), “specified share” means a share in the
-- src:6697 | company, by whatever name called which, but for that subsection,
-- src:6698 | does not entitle the holder thereof to the right to vote at a general
-- src:6699 | meeting of the company.
@ref s 64(5) (src:6696-6699)
GIVEN `the share is a share in the company, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for subsection (4) the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(5) "specified share" the share is a specified share` MEANS
    IF `the share is a share in the company, by whatever name called` AND `but for subsection (4) the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""specified share" means a share in the company, by whatever name called which, but for that subsection, does not entitle the holder thereof to the right to vote at a general meeting of the company" (a "means" definition)

-- (6) saving of rights under section 74.
-- src:6703 | (6) This section does not operate so as to limit or derogate from the
-- src:6704 | rights of any person under section 74.
@ref s 64(6) (src:6703-6704)
GIVEN `the right is a right of a person under section 74` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(6) section 64 limits or derogates from the right` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right of a person under section 74`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not operate so as to limit or derogate from the rights of any person under section 74"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rights of any person under section 74" -- another right is not covered

§ `Section 64A: issue of shares with different voting rights by a public company`

-- (1) different classes in a public company: "only if". JUST FALSE where a condition fails.
-- src:6710 | 64A.—(1) Different classes of shares in a public company may be
-- src:6711 | issued only if —
-- src:6716 | (a) the issue of the class or classes of shares is provided for in
-- src:6717 | the constitution of the public company; and
-- src:6719 | (b) the constitution of the public company sets out in respect of
-- src:6720 | each class of shares the rights attached to that class of
-- src:6721 | shares.
@ref s 64A(1) (src:6710-6721)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue of the class or classes of shares is provided for in the constitution of the public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the public company sets out in respect of each class of shares the rights attached to that class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A(1) different classes of shares in the public company may be issued` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Different classes of shares in a public company" -- a private company is not covered (subsection (6) says so for the private company)
    ELSE (IF `the issue of the class or classes of shares is provided for in the constitution of the public company` AND `the constitution of the public company sets out in respect of each class of shares the rights attached to that class of shares`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be issued only if" -- an "only if" the constitution does not meet

-- (2) special, limited, conditional or no voting rights: a grant, subject to the conditions of (1)(a) and (b).
-- src:6725 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1) but subject to the conditions of
-- src:6726 | subsection (1)(a) and (b), shares in a public company may —
-- src:6728 | (a) confer special, limited, or conditional voting rights; or
-- src:6730 | (b) not confer voting rights.
@ref s 64A(2) (src:6725-6730)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or confer no voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A(2) the shares in the public company may confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the conditions of subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met` AND `the shares confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or confer no voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares in a public company may ... subject to the conditions of subsection (1)(a) and (b)" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1); section 64A(1) answers the class itself (fork F-RT2)

-- (3) the bar on issuing such shares without a special resolution. JUST TRUE is barred.
-- src:6734 | (3) Despite anything in subsection (1) or (2), a public company
-- src:6735 | must not undertake any issuance of shares in the public company that
-- src:6736 | confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or that confers no
-- src:6737 | voting rights unless it is approved by the members of the public
-- src:6738 | company by special resolution.
@ref s 64A(3) (src:6734-6738)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuance confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or confers no voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuance is approved by the members of the public company by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A(3) the public company is barred from the issuance` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR (NOT `the issuance confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or confers no voting rights`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a public company must not undertake any issuance of shares in the public company that confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or that confers no voting rights" -- another company or another issuance is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the issuance is approved by the members of the public company by special resolution`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is approved by the members of the public company by special resolution" -- the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 64A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 64A(3) undertake an issuance of shares that confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights, without approval by special resolution`

@ref s 64A(3) (src:6734-6738)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 64A act`
`s 64A(3) a public company must not issue shares with special, limited, conditional or no voting rights without approval by special resolution` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 64A(3) undertake an issuance of shares that confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights, without approval by special resolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company undertook an issuance of shares that confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights, without approval by the members by special resolution"

-- (4) the notice of a general meeting. JUST TRUE is a notice that falls short.
-- src:6742 | (4) Where a public company has one or more classes of shares that
-- src:6743 | confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or that confer no
-- src:6744 | voting rights, the notice of any general meeting required to be given
-- src:6745 | to a person entitled to receive notice of the meeting must specify the
-- src:6746 | special, limited or conditional voting rights, or the absence of voting
-- src:6747 | rights, in respect of each such class of shares.
@ref s 64A(4) (src:6742-6747)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has one or more classes of shares that confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or that confer no voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of the general meeting specifies the special, limited or conditional voting rights, or the absence of voting rights, in respect of each such class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A(4) the notice of the general meeting falls short of what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the company has one or more classes of shares that confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or that confer no voting rights`
    THEN (IF `the notice of the general meeting specifies the special, limited or conditional voting rights, or the absence of voting rights, in respect of each such class of shares`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice of any general meeting required to be given to a person entitled to receive notice of the meeting must specify the special, limited or conditional voting rights" -- the notice specifies them: the duty is done
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a public company has one or more classes of shares that confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or that confer no voting rights, the notice ... must specify" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise

-- (5) saving of rights under section 74.
-- src:6751 | (5) This section does not operate so as to limit or derogate from the
-- src:6752 | rights of any person under section 74.
@ref s 64A(5) (src:6751-6752)
GIVEN `the right is a right of a person under section 74` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A(5) section 64A limits or derogates from the right` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right of a person under section 74`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not operate so as to limit or derogate from the rights of any person under section 74"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rights of any person under section 74" -- another right is not covered

-- (6) the private company's right to issue classes, subject to its constitution.
-- src:6756 | (6) Nothing in this section affects the right of a private company,
-- src:6757 | subject to its constitution, to issue shares of different classes,
-- src:6758 | including shares conferring special, limited or conditional voting
-- src:6759 | rights or no voting rights, as the case may be.
@ref s 64A(6) (src:6756-6759)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the private company forbids the issue of shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A(6) the private company may issue shares of different classes, including shares with special, limited or conditional voting rights or no voting rights` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the right of a private company" -- a public company is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the constitution of the private company forbids the issue of shares of different classes`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the right of a private company, subject to its constitution, to issue shares of different classes" -- the constitution forbids it (fork F-RT3)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 65: differences in calls and payments, and reserve liability`

-- (1) the three powers, if the constitution so authorises. The power is a choice; (c) carries its own condition.
-- src:6768 | 65.—(1) A company if so authorised by its constitution may —
-- src:6770 | (a) make arrangements on the issue of shares for varying the
-- src:6771 | amounts and times of payment of calls as between
-- src:6772 | shareholders;
-- src:6774 | (b) accept from any member the whole or a part of the amount
-- src:6775 | remaining unpaid on any shares although no part of that
-- src:6776 | amount has been called up; and
-- src:6778 | (c) pay dividends in proportion to the amount paid up on each
-- src:6779 | share where a larger amount is paid up on some shares than
-- src:6780 | on others.
@ref s 65(1) (src:6768-6780)
DECLARE `s 65(1) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 65(1)(a) make arrangements on the issue of shares for varying the amounts and times of payment of calls as between shareholders`
    `s 65(1)(b) accept from a member the whole or a part of the amount remaining unpaid on any shares although no part of that amount has been called up`
    `s 65(1)(c) pay dividends in proportion to the amount paid up on each share`
        HAS `s 65(1)(c) a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 65(1) some other power`

@ref s 65(1) (src:6768-6780)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company authorises the company to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `s 65(1) power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the constitution of the company authorises the company to exercise the power`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company if so authorised by its constitution may" -- a grant whose "if" gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1); the subsection does not say the company may not
    ELSE CONSIDER power
         WHEN `s 65(1)(a) make arrangements on the issue of shares for varying the amounts and times of payment of calls as between shareholders` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 65(1)(b) accept from a member the whole or a part of the amount remaining unpaid on any shares although no part of that amount has been called up` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 65(1)(c) pay dividends in proportion to the amount paid up on each share` larger THEN (IF larger THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others" -- the power is given for that case
         WHEN `s 65(1) some other power` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) to (c) are listed without "only"

-- (2) reserve liability: the grant, then its effect, then the saving of earlier rights.
-- src:6786 | (2) A limited company may by special resolution determine that
-- src:6787 | any portion of its share capital which has not been already called up is
-- src:6788 | not capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes
-- src:6789 | of the company being wound up, and thereupon that portion of its
-- src:6790 | share capital is not capable of being called up except in the event and
-- src:6791 | for the purposes of the company being wound up, but no such
-- src:6792 | resolution affects the rights of any person acquired before the passing
-- src:6793 | of the resolution.
@ref s 65(2) (src:6786-6793)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has passed a special resolution that a portion of its share capital which has not been already called up is not capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2) the limited company may determine that a portion of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called up except in a winding up` MEANS
    IF `the company is a limited company` AND `the company has passed a special resolution that a portion of its share capital which has not been already called up is not capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A limited company may by special resolution determine" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

@ref s 65(2) (src:6786-6793)
GIVEN `the company has passed the special resolution described in section 65(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion of the share capital had not been called up when the resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2) the portion is capable of being called up other than in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up` MEANS
    IF `the company has passed the special resolution described in section 65(2)` AND `the portion of the share capital had not been called up when the resolution was passed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "thereupon that portion of its share capital is not capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any portion of its share capital which has not been already called up" -- another portion is not covered

@ref s 65(2) (src:6786-6793)
GIVEN `the person acquired the rights before the passing of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2) the resolution affects the rights of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person acquired the rights before the passing of the resolution`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no such resolution affects the rights of any person acquired before the passing of the resolution"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rights of any person acquired before the passing of the resolution" -- a right acquired later is not covered

§ `Section 66: share warrants`

-- (1) the bar on issuing a bearer share warrant. JUST TRUE is barred.
-- src:6797 | 66.—(1) A company must not issue any share warrant stating that
-- src:6798 | the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares therein specified and
-- src:6799 | which enables the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant.
@ref s 66(1) (src:6797-6799)
GIVEN `the warrant states that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares therein specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant enables the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(1) the company is barred from issuing the share warrant` MEANS
    IF `the warrant states that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares therein specified` AND `the warrant enables the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any share warrant stating that the bearer of the warrant is entitled to the shares therein specified and which enables the shares to be transferred by delivery of the warrant" -- another instrument is not covered

DECLARE `s 66 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(1) issue a share warrant stating that the bearer is entitled to the shares specified and enabling them to be transferred by delivery of the warrant`
    `s 66(4) cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period`

@ref s 66(1) (src:6797-6799)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 66 act`
`s 66(1) a company must not issue a share warrant to bearer` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 66(1) issue a share warrant stating that the bearer is entitled to the shares specified and enabling them to be transferred by delivery of the warrant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company issued a share warrant stating that the bearer is entitled to the shares specified and enabling them to be transferred by delivery of the warrant"

-- (2) the bearer's right to surrender in the 2-year period after 1 July 2015.
-- src:6801 | (2) The bearer of a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967
-- src:6802 | is, in the 2‑year period after 1 July 2015, entitled to surrender it for
-- src:6803 | cancellation and to have the bearer’s name entered in the register of
-- src:6804 | members.
@ref s 66(2) (src:6801-6804)
`s 66(2) the day 1 July 2015` MEANS Date 1 7 2015

@ref s 66(2) (src:6801-6804)
`s 66(2) the day 29 December 1967` MEANS Date 29 12 1967

@ref s 66(2) (src:6801-6804)
GIVEN `the day the share warrant was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` MEANS
    IF `the day the share warrant was issued` AT LEAST `s 66(2) the day 29 December 1967`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The bearer of a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967" -- a warrant issued on or after that day is not covered (fork F-RT4: the subsection says "before")
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `s 66(2) the day 1 July 2015` `the day on which the question is asked` 2 Years
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the 2-year period after 1 July 2015, entitled to surrender it" -- outside the period the text fixes (periods ruling (a); fork F-RT4)

-- (3) the company's responsibility for loss when it enters the bearer's name without surrender.
-- src:6808 | (3) The company is responsible for any loss incurred by any person
-- src:6809 | by reason of the company entering in the register the name of a bearer
-- src:6810 | of a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 in respect of the
-- src:6815 | shares therein specified without the warrant being surrendered and
-- src:6816 | cancelled.
@ref s 66(3) (src:6808-6816)
GIVEN `the share warrant was issued before 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company entered in the register the name of the bearer of the share warrant in respect of the shares therein specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant was surrendered and cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person incurred loss by reason of the company entering the name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(3) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person` MEANS
    IF    `the share warrant was issued before 29 December 1967`
      AND `the company entered in the register the name of the bearer of the share warrant in respect of the shares therein specified`
      AND (NOT `the warrant was surrendered and cancelled`)
      AND `the person incurred loss by reason of the company entering the name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any loss incurred by any person by reason of the company entering in the register the name of a bearer of a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 ... without the warrant being surrendered and cancelled" -- another entry or another loss is not covered

-- (4) the duty to cancel, and the company's freedom from responsibility for the cancellation. The 2-year period ends 1 July 2017 (keel convention P4).
-- src:6820 | (4) A company must cancel any share warrant which is issued by a
-- src:6821 | company before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the
-- src:6822 | expiry of the 2‑year period mentioned in subsection (2), and the
-- src:6823 | company is not responsible for any loss incurred by any person by
-- src:6824 | reason of such cancellation.
@ref s 66(4) (src:6820-6824)
GIVEN `the day the share warrant was issued` IS A DATE
      `the share warrant is accounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(4) the share warrant is one the company must cancel` MEANS
    IF `the day the share warrant was issued` AT LEAST `s 66(2) the day 29 December 1967`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any share warrant which is issued by a company before 29 December 1967" -- a warrant issued on or after that day is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the share warrant is accounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period mentioned in subsection (2)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any share warrant ... that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period" -- an accounted-for warrant is outside the duty (marginal reading (a); fork F-RT5)
          ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `s 66(2) the day 1 July 2015` 2 Years
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period" -- the period has not yet expired (periods ruling (a))

@ref s 66(4) (src:6820-6824)
GIVEN `the share warrant was cancelled as subsection (4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(4) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person by reason of the cancellation` MEANS
    IF `the share warrant was cancelled as subsection (4) requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is not responsible for any loss incurred by any person by reason of such cancellation"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason of such cancellation" -- another loss is not covered

-- The duty to cancel has no deadline of its own in the text: the period names when the warrant becomes one to cancel, not when the cancelling is due (fork F-RT5). With no WITHIN it cannot reach BREACH (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sga1)").
@ref s 66(4) (src:6820-6824)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 66 act`
`s 66(4) a company must cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 66(4) cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 66(4) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not cancel the share warrant" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 67: use of share capital to pay the expenses of issuing new shares`

-- (1) the power.
-- src:6831 | 67.—(1) A company may use its share capital to pay any expenses
-- src:6832 | (including brokerage or commission) incurred directly in the issue of
-- src:6833 | new shares.
@ref s 67(1) (src:6831-6833)
GIVEN `the expenses (including brokerage or commission) were incurred directly in the issue of new shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1) the company may use its share capital to pay the expenses` MEANS
    IF `the expenses (including brokerage or commission) were incurred directly in the issue of new shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any expenses (including brokerage or commission) incurred directly in the issue of new shares" -- other expenses are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (2) the payment is not a reduction.
-- src:6837 | (2) A payment made under subsection (1) is not to be taken as
-- src:6838 | reducing the amount of share capital of the company.
@ref s 67(2) (src:6837-6838)
GIVEN `the payment is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(2) the payment is to be taken as reducing the amount of share capital of the company` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A payment made under subsection (1) is not to be taken as reducing the amount of share capital of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A payment made under subsection (1)" -- another payment is not covered

§ `Section 68: issue of shares for no consideration`

-- src:6844 | 68. A company having a share capital may issue shares for which
-- src:6845 | no consideration is payable to the issuing company.
@ref s 68 (src:6844-6845)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no consideration is payable to the issuing company for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68 the company may issue the shares for no consideration` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital` AND `no consideration is payable to the issuing company for the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company having a share capital may issue shares for which no consideration is payable to the issuing company" -- a company with no share capital is not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
